25 0 obj
<<
/Title (Abstract  The escalating integration of the Internet of Things \(IoT\) into the fundamental fabric of modern infrastructure has necessitated a transformative approach to data security, particularly as the network of connected devices is projected to exceed 41 billion by the year 2027. This report presents an exhaustive investigation into a novel cryptographic paradigm that synthesizes the structural properties of graph theory with the adaptive capabilities of machine learning \(ML\) to secure bidirectional data exchange between IoT nodes. At the center of this research is the Index Difference Graph \(IDG\), a newly formulated mathematical structure that serves as the foundation for the Index Difference Modular Cryptographic \(IDMC\) algorithm. The IDG model facilitates a high-entropy secret key architecture where vertex positions and labeling indices are predetermined according to specific topological conditions, achieving a linear computational complexity of O\(n\) that is ideal for resource-constrained embedded systems.  By comparing the contemporary findings of the 2025 Index Difference Graph research with established standards such as AES-128, ASCON, and ECC-based hybrid frameworks documented in IEEE and ResearchGate, this study elucidates a hybrid security model designated as the Intelligent Graph-ML Hybrid Architecture \(IGMH\). This proposed framework integrates)
/Dest [10 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 7 0 R
/Next 526 0 R
>>
endobj
26 0 obj
<<
/Title (Moving forward, the strategic focus for cryptography experts and IoT architects must shift toward "crypto-agility" and structural security. The structural complexity of Index Difference Graphs provides a formidable barrier to the "Harvest Now, Decrypt Later" strategy, ensuring that data remains confidential even as quantum computing capabilities expand. Furthermore, the continuous improvement of machine learning models for real-time threat detection will ensure that IoT ecosystems can autonomously adapt to an increasingly hostile cyber landscape, safeguarding the privacy, integrity, and availability of the global connected infrastructure.)
/Dest [21 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 7 0 R
/Prev 527 0 R
>>
endobj
