/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 333 0 R
/T (Integration with machine learning enhances this structural foundation in two ways. First, an Autoencoder Neural Network is utilized for secure key generation. Instead of relying on predictable pseudo-random number generators, the Autoencoder is trained on high-entropy datasets \(such as MNIST\) to generate unique, robust cryptographic seeds that define the initial vertex positions and labeling indices of the IDG. Second, an optimized Artificial Neural Network \(ANN\) is integrated into the broker node to serve as a real-time anomaly detection engine. This model classifies incoming traffic into legitimate and malicious categories \(e.g., DoS, flooding, or malformed packets\) with a demonstrated accuracy of over 90%, providing a layer of security that encryption alone cannot provide. )
/E (Integration with machine learning enhances this structural foundation in two ways. First, an Autoencoder Neural Network is utilized for secure key generation. Instead of relying on predictable pseudo-random number generators, the Autoencoder is trained on high-entropy datasets \(such as MNIST\) to generate unique, robust cryptographic seeds that define the initial vertex positions and labeling indices of the IDG. Second, an optimized Artificial Neural Network \(ANN\) is integrated into the broker node to serve as a real-time anomaly detection engine. This model classifies incoming traffic into legitimate and malicious categories \(e.g., DoS, flooding, or malformed packets\) with a demonstrated accuracy of over 90%, providing a layer of security that encryption alone cannot provide. )
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
371 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 333 0 R
/T (The final layer of the IGMH framework is a Moving Target Defense \(MTD\) strategy governed by a Deep Reinforcement Learning \(DRL\) agent. This agent, part of the "REACT" \(Randomized Encryption with AI-Controlled Targeting\) sub-module, dynamically randomizes encryption patterns and re-labels the IDG structural key after each successful transmission. By continuously shifting the attack surface and updating encryption keys in 12-50 millisecond cycles, the IGMH framework effectively thwarts side-channel attacks that rely on gathering a large number of traces for a single key. This hybrid approach ensures that the security system is not only mathematically strong but also behaviorally intelligent and operationally agile. )
/E (The final layer of the IGMH framework is a Moving Target Defense \(MTD\) strategy governed by a Deep Reinforcement Learning \(DRL\) agent. This agent, part of the "REACT" \(Randomized Encryption with AI-Controlled Targeting\) sub-module, dynamically randomizes encryption patterns and re-labels the IDG structural key after each successful transmission. By continuously shifting the attack surface and updating encryption keys in 12-50 millisecond cycles, the IGMH framework effectively thwarts side-channel attacks that rely on gathering a large number of traces for a single key. This hybrid approach ensures that the security system is not only mathematically strong but also behaviorally intelligent and operationally agile. )
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [3]
>>
