/P 340 0 R
/T (Data synthesized from. The analysis indicates that while AES-128 provides strong security, its round-based structure on resource-constrained devices without dedicated hardware accelerators. In contrast, the IDMC algorithm achieves high security through the structural complexity of the graph labeling, but with  a much simpler modular operation that executes in sub-millisecond time. )
/E (Data synthesized from. The analysis indicates that while AES-128 provides strong security, its round-based structure on resource-constrained devices without dedicated hardware accelerators. In contrast, the IDMC algorithm achieves high security through the structural complexity of the graph labeling, but with  a much simpler modular operation that executes in sub-millisecond time. )
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
505 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 340 0 R
/T (The IGMH model's adaptive nature further differentiates it from "static" ciphers like ASCON or SPECK. By integrating ANN-based threat detection, the IGMH framework can adjust its security parameters in real time. For instance, during a high-threat event, the system can switch to a more complex Double Triangular Snake graph, while reverting to a simple Path graph during low-power, routine operations. This "adaptive hybrid" approach provides up to 47% energy savings and 38% latency reductions compared to static security protocols. )
/E (The IGMH model's adaptive nature further differentiates it from "static" ciphers like ASCON or SPECK. By integrating ANN-based threat detection, the IGMH framework can adjust its security parameters in real time. For instance, during a high-threat event, the system can switch to a more complex Double Triangular Snake graph, while reverting to a simple Path graph during low-power, routine operations. This "adaptive hybrid" approach provides up to 47% energy savings and 38% latency reductions compared to static security protocols. )
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
