/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 341 0 R
/T (Conclusion  The evolution of the Internet of Things has brought the industry to a critical crossroad where the proliferation of edge devices has outpaced the development of secure, efficient, and quantum-ready cryptographic standards. This research report has demonstrated that the synthesis of graph-theoretic structural labeling and machine learning-driven adaptive defense offers a powerful solution to this dilemma. The Index Difference Graph \(IDG\) and the associated IDMC algorithm provide a revolutionary alternative to traditional block ciphers, achieving linear O\(n\) complexity and immense brute-force resistance by treating graph topology as a mathematical secret key. )
/E (Conclusion  The evolution of the Internet of Things has brought the industry to a critical crossroad where the proliferation of edge devices has outpaced the development of secure, efficient, and quantum-ready cryptographic standards. This research report has demonstrated that the synthesis of graph-theoretic structural labeling and machine learning-driven adaptive defense offers a powerful solution to this dilemma. The Index Difference Graph \(IDG\) and the associated IDMC algorithm provide a revolutionary alternative to traditional block ciphers, achieving linear O\(n\) complexity and immense brute-force resistance by treating graph topology as a mathematical secret key. )
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
