/Title (Introduction  The contemporary digital era is defined by the pervasive growth of interconnected devices, a phenomenon that has transcended simple home automation to encompass critical national infrastructures, healthcare ecosystems, and complex industrial supply chains. As these systems collect and transmit vast quantities of sensitive data, they expose an ever-expanding attack surface to sophisticated adversaries. Traditional cryptographic paradigms, while mathematically robust, often fail to address the unique operational requirements of IoT environments, where devices are frequently characterized by limited processing power, restricted memory capacity, and finite energy supplies. The year 2024 has marked a significant turning point in this landscape, with the conclusion of the NIST lightweight cryptography standardization process and the rising urgency of preparing for the post-quantum horizon.)
/Dest [11 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 7 0 R
