/Title (Senior cryptography research experts and security professionals now face the dual challenge of ensuring immediate data confidentiality while building "crypto-agile" systems capable of resisting both classical and emerging quantum attacks. Graph theory has recently gained prominence in this field, providing a mathematical framework for organizing and encrypting data through complex labeling techniques that are structurally difficult to reverse-engineer. The synthesis of graph-theoretic properties with cryptographic operations allows for the creation of non-standard encryption algorithms that offer a formidable defense against conventional attacks such as frequency analysis and exhaustive key searches.)
/Dest [11 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 7 0 R
