/Title (Furthermore, the integration of machine learning into these cryptographic frameworks provides an intelligent layer of defense that static algorithms cannot achieve. Machine learning models, such as Artificial Neural Networks \(ANN\), can function as real-time gatekeepers, analyzing network traffic for anomalous patterns that may indicate a side-channel attack or a denial-of-service \(DoS\) attempt. The synergy between the structural security of IDG and the behavioral intelligence of ML models defines the future of secure IoT communication, particularly in 2-node simulations where edge devices must autonomously manage their security posture in hostile network environments.)
