/Title (Resource constraints remain the primary barrier to robust encryption. Standard algorithms like AES-128 or RSA-2048 impose substantial computational and memory overheads that can lead to increased latency in real-time systems, such as medical heart-rate monitors or industrial controllers. In the clinical context of the Internet of Medical Things \(IoMT\), high-latency encryption can disrupt the reliability of critical alerts, potentially compromising patient safety. Moreover, the energy consumption required for complex cryptographic operations can rapidly deplete the battery life of remote sensors, leading to maintenance failures and data loss.)
/Dest [12 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 7 0 R
/Prev 1344 0 R
/Next 1348 0 R
>>
endobj
