/Title (Current research also highlights the rising threat of Side-Channel Attacks \(SCA\), which exploit physical signals such as power fluctuations, electromagnetic radiation, and timing variances to extract secret keys. Mathematical security does not guarantee implementation security; a mathematically "unbreakable" cipher may still leak its key through the physical characteristics of the hardware it runs on. This is particularly problematic for lightweight cryptographic \(LWC\) primitives implemented in unrolled architectures, where low latency is prioritized over side-channel resistance.)
/Dest [12 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 7 0 R
/Prev 1346 0 R
/Next 1350 0 R
>>
