/Title (Finally, the lack of adaptive security frameworks means that most IoT devices operate with a static security posture, regardless of the actual threat level or device status. A device with a low battery in a low-threat environment may still be forced to run high-overhead encryption, while a device under active attack may lack the intelligence to strengthen its security parameters dynamically. There is a critical need for a hybrid approach that integrates structural graph-based security with machine learning to provide an adaptive, resource-efficient, and quantum-ready defense for network-based IoT data exchange.)
/Dest [12 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 7 0 R
/Prev 1350 0 R
/Next 1354 0 R
>>
endobj
1353 0 obj
<<
/Title (The IGMH model's adaptive nature further differentiates it from "static" ciphers like ASCON or SPECK. By integrating ANN-based threat detection, the IGMH framework can adjust its security parameters in real time. For instance, during a high-threat event, the system can switch to a more complex Double Triangular Snake graph, while reverting to a simple Path graph during low-power, routine operations. This "adaptive hybrid" approach provides up to 47% energy savings and 38% latency reductions compared to static security protocols.)
/Dest [20 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 7 0 R
/Prev 1355 0 R
/Next 1351 0 R
>>
