/Title (Integration with machine learning enhances this structural foundation in two ways. First, an Autoencoder Neural Network is utilized for secure key generation. Instead of relying on predictable pseudo-random number generators, the Autoencoder is trained on high-entropy datasets \(such as MNIST\) to generate unique, robust cryptographic seeds that define the initial vertex positions and labeling indices of the IDG. Second, an optimized Artificial Neural Network \(ANN\) is integrated into the broker node to serve as a real-time anomaly detection engine. This model classifies incoming traffic into legitimate and malicious categories \(e.g., DoS, flooding, or malformed packets\) with a demonstrated accuracy of over 90%, providing a layer of security that encryption alone cannot provide.)
/Dest [13 0 R /Fit]
