/Title (The final layer of the IGMH framework is a Moving Target Defense \(MTD\) strategy governed by a Deep Reinforcement Learning \(DRL\) agent. This agent, part of the "REACT" \(Randomized Encryption with AI-Controlled Targeting\) sub-module, dynamically randomizes encryption patterns and re-labels the IDG structural key after each successful transmission. By continuously shifting the attack surface and updating encryption keys in 12-50 millisecond cycles, the IGMH framework effectively thwarts side-channel attacks that rely on gathering a large number of traces for a single key. This hybrid approach ensures that the security system is not only mathematically strong but also behaviorally intelligent and operationally agile.)
