/Title (Machine Learning Integration and Anomaly Detection  The second phase of the methodology involves embedding machine learning into the security lifecycle. The Autoencoder model is used to generate the seeds for the IDG positioning. During the training phase, the model learns to compress and reconstruct complex patterns, and the resulting latent representation is hashed \(e.g., using SHA-512\) to produce a 512-bit seed. This seed is then used by both the sender \(Node A\) and receiver \(Node B\) to derive identical graph labeling sequences without transmitting the key itself.)
