/Title (Concurrently, an Artificial Neural Network \(ANN\) is deployed at the network broker to monitor MQTT traffic. The model is trained on a standardized IoT dataset \(e.g., MQTTset\) which includes legitimate traffic and five common attack vectors: DoS, brute-force, malformed packets, SlowITe, and flooding. The ANN architecture consists of an input layer for traffic features, multiple hidden layers optimized through trial-and-error, and an output layer for multi-class classification. This model functions as a real-time gatekeeper, granting access only to connections that do not exhibit malicious signatures.)
